      <div class="acc" data-acc>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1" id="faq-b1">What is raw feeding?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b1"><div><p>Raw feeding means meals made from raw muscle meat, organ meat, ground bone, vegetables and a little fruit, instead of cooked kibble. Our recipes are complete meals: you thaw a pack and serve it, nothing to add.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-2" id="faq-b2">How do I switch from kibble?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b2"><div><p>Most dogs switch over 7 to 10 days. Start with a quarter of the meal raw and the rest the old food, and raise the raw part every two or three days. Keep the portion size the same and slow down if stools get soft. Cats often take longer: mix in a spoonful at a time.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-3" id="faq-b3">How do I store and thaw the packs?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b3"><div><p>Keep packs in the freezer at −18 °C for up to six months. Thaw one in the fridge overnight and use it within three days. Do not thaw in the microwave or in hot water, and do not refreeze a thawed pack.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-4" id="faq-b4">How much should I feed?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b4"><div><p>Most adult dogs eat 2 to 3 % of their body weight a day; puppies and kittens eat more. The meal finder above gives you a starting point. Weigh your pet every two weeks and adjust by about 10 %, and ask your vet if your pet has a health condition.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-5" id="faq-b5">Do you deliver?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b5"><div><p>We deliver around Portland on Tuesdays and Fridays in insulated boxes with ice packs, or you can pick up at the kitchen on Dock Road. Send an order request and we confirm the day and the total by email or text. You pay on delivery or pick-up.</p></div></div></div>
        <div class="acc-item open"><h3><button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-6" id="faq-b6">Is raw food safe to handle?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></button></h3><div class="acc-panel" id="faq-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="faq-b6"><div><p>Handle it like the raw meat you cook for yourself: wash hands, bowls and surfaces with hot soapy water after serving, and keep raw food away from small children. Every batch is frozen within hours of making and stays frozen until it reaches you.</p></div></div></div>
